    "scope": "Create, read, edit, reschedule and delete your own titled appointments with a start and an end date-time in a fixed UTC+08:00 offset and optional location and notes, shown on a real seven-column month grid whose schedule is persisted locally across restarts and navigable back into past months.",
    "summary": "OpenCode Go静态研究与独立会话审阅；Target proposal: implement the leaf as a single-user desktop GUI application in Python 3 using only the standard library - Tkinter for the seven-column month frame, the day cells, the event blocks and the appointment editor - with one local JSON document as the persistent store, a fixed UTC+08:00 offset and no accounts, sync, recurrence, all-day mode or notifications; the upstream elementary/calendar project (GPL-3.0) is used only as a structural reference for the grid and event model and no upstream code is copied.",
    "task_id": "full-leaf-auxiliary-2026-10-21-calendar-application-attempt-1",
    "unknowns": [
      "upstream not_run",
      "auxiliary independent static review passed; runtime not_run",
      "Only the month frame is implemented; there is no day, week, agenda or year view, and the upstream week-number toggle is deliberately not reproduced.",
      "Rescheduling is done through the editor's date-time fields rather than by dragging a block to another day, so the upstream drag-and-drop reschedule is not reproduced.",
      "The upstream Evolution Data Server / iCalendar source layer, calendar colours, calendars sidebar, context menus and libical interop are out of scope; the store is one local JSON document.",
      "All instants use a fixed UTC+08:00 offset with no daylight-saving handling and no time-zone switch, so appointments do not follow a machine zone change.",
      "There is no undo/redo, no search, no import/export, no recurring event, no all-day mode, no reminders, no attendee or invitation data.",
      "The widget-tree half of the acceptance probe is reported as NOT_RUN on a machine without a graphical display; the model/store half still runs there.",
      "The target code is not present in this workspace, so the probe is expected to fail loudly rather than pass until the implementation is written.",
      "No upstream code was copied; the GPL-3.0 upstream project was read as a structural reference only."
    ]
  },
